## Traveling salesman (traveling-salesman), generated from the Rosie teaching script (english-input.txt) under the world conventions.
##
## Instructor statements used (numbers as in english-input.txt):
##   5. If a clear location is adjacent to a red block then you can move the red block onto the clear location and move a clear available blue block onto a location that was below the red block.
##   6. If a block is not on a location then it is available.
##   7. If a location is not below an object then it is clear.
##   8. If a location is next to an object but it is not diagonal with the object then it is adjacent to the object.
##  11. The goal is that all locations are covered and a red block is adjacent to a green location.
##  13. If a location is below an object then it is covered.
## World: init-tourrc.world (a 4 by 3 grid; the red block on one location, eleven blue blocks in a stack)
##
## Translation (tools/rosie-language.md gives the general reading; the assumption ledger is in README.md):
##   - Operator move-salesman ( argument1 = the red block, argument2 = the clear location),
##     statement 5; adjacent (statement 8) is a static relation between locations (A-G1).
##   - "The solution has eleven steps" (statement 9) is checked against the plans, not used.
##   - available (not on a location) and clear are maintained one-argument relations; the blue blocks start in a stack, and the
##     clear available blue block is its top, found by the applications (A-G4).
##   - covered (below an object) is expanded in place; the goal is expanded over the locations of the world file and adds a red block on a location adjacent to a green location.
## Matching hints for learned rules (World-Conventions L3-095, L11-009): many-valued attributes, sized from the initial world.
production optimize-attribute object 25
production optimize-attribute on 11
production optimize-attribute below 11
production optimize-attribute clear 13
production optimize-attribute available 11
production optimize-attribute adjacent 34


## Propose initialize-traveling-salesman when its conditions below hold.
sp {traveling-salesman*propose*initialize-traveling-salesman
   (state <s> ^superstate nil ^world <w> -^name)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <o> + >)
   (<o> ^name initialize-traveling-salesman ^task-operator false)
}

sp {traveling-salesman*apply*initialize-traveling-salesman
